## Limits and next gate

The full collector source and its SHA were inspected statically, along with the focused accepted H3c collector sections and its independent review. Ruff and in-memory compile PASS were reported by the controller; this reviewer did not rerun them. No moving P2 production source was inspected. No source imports, collector execution, archive readers/summaries, tests, probes, synthetic inputs or artifacts, preparation, campaign, provider/API, Docker/evaluation, credentials/environment values, or Git mutations occurred. Only this report was written.

Execution remains gated on final independent P4 source approval and a genuine reviewed-source-authority file for that approved freeze. The approved invocation should retain the accepted collector's bytecode suppression and run while those sources and archives are held unchanged. The before/after maps establish observed preservation, not an atomic snapshot or protection against concurrent changes between hashing and imports. Actual returned summary compatibility remains unverified until that later authorized run.
